Upload Installable APK Artifact\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        with:\n          name: Chandra-Printers-Release-APK\n          path: build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk\n\n      - name: Create GitHub Release with APK Download\n        uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v1\n        if: startsWith(github.ref, \u0027refs/tags/\u0027)\n        with:\n          files: build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n```\n\n### How to download your ready APK from this pipeline:\n1. When you push the code to GitHub, click the **Actions** tab in your repository.\n2. Click on the latest workflow run: **Build CHANDRA PRINTERS Android APK**.\n3. Under the **Artifacts** section at the bottom, click **Chandra-Printers-Release-APK**.\n4. The zip file contains the fully compiled `app-release.apk` ready to install directly on any Android smartphone.\n\n---\n\n# Part 4: Building the APK Locally (Terminal / Command Line)\n\nIf you have Flutter installed on your PC or Mac, follow these steps to compile the APK in 2 minutes:\n\n### 1. Test in Debug Mode on your connected phone:\n```bash\nflutter run\n```\n\n### 2. Build the Production Release APK:\n```bash\nflutter build apk --release\n```\nThe compiled APK will be located at:\n```text\nbuild/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk\n```\n\n### 3. (Optional) Build a Signed Keystore for Google Play Store:\nGenerate the production keystore:\n```bash\nkeytool -genkey -v -keystore chandra-release.jks -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias chandraprinters\n```\n\nReference it in your `android/key.properties`:\n```properties\nstorePassword\u003dYourKeystorePassword\nkeyPassword\u003dYourKeyPassword\nkeyAlias\u003dchandraprinters\nstoreFile\u003d/path/to/chandra-release.jks\n```\n\nThen run:\n```bash\nflutter build appbundle --release\n```\n\n---\n\n# Part 5: Android Installation Instructions (For End Users)\n\n1. Transfer the generated `app-